Mission A-38 finding: docs/verification/VERIFICATION_REGISTRY.json did not
exist anywhere in the repo (DEF-A38-01). De-facto evidence lives scattered in
markdown (RELEASE_GATE_EVIDENCE.md, HANDOFF, audit reports) citing stale SHAs
(da13943@2026-09-09, 0a208f8/1a73c52@2026-09-13, undated audit docs) - none
machine-verifiable, none valid for current HEAD.

Structural fix (no item was greened):
- docs/verification/VERIFICATION_REGISTRY.json (schema 1.0.0): 9 mandatory
  fields per item (requirement/head_sha/command/exit_code/artifact/reviewer/
  timestamp/runtime/limitation) + status enum VERIFIED_E3|DEFECT_OPEN|STALE|
  BLOCKED|NOT_VERIFIED. CERTIFIED forbidden by policy.
- Fresh E3 evidence executed at product tree 66928be (this session):
  VR-002 smoke 547/547 exit0, VR-003 semantic-layer 33/33 exit0,
  VR-004 api-runner 30/30 exit0 -> VERIFIED_E3 with artifacts under
  docs/verification/evidence/66928be/ (COMMAND/HEAD/DATE/RUNTIME/EXIT_CODE
  headers).
- VR-001 run.js recorded honestly as DEFECT_OPEN exit=1: first run from
  pristine checkout fails 'build output byte-identical to index.html'
  (34/35), self-heals on run 2 (35/35). Committed index.html is not
  byte-identical with build.js output in canonical runtime (DEF-A38-02).
  NOT greened.
- Historical evidence registered as STALE (VR-201..205), explicitly NOT
  VERIFIED for current HEAD; two audit docs record no exact SHA (DEF-A38-03).
- Out-of-repo/unpushed-branch evidence (arena9 5f0af4e, arena-iqa 871ff05
  battery 263/263) registered NOT_VERIFIED for main.
- Unrunnable-here requirements registered BLOCKED with reasons (CI/Actions
  billing, live PG, Redis failover, DAST/pentest, k6, remote parity).

Regression gate: tests/verification-registry.test.js (140 checks):
- VERIFIED_E3 requires exit_code=0 + artifact with full header + 40-hex SHA
  resolvable + product-tree (server/, src/, index.html, build.js, sw.js,
  manifest.json, authz/) unchanged since evidence SHA (auto-stale otherwise).
- Artifact<->SHA binding defeats retroactive revalidation by SHA edit.
- Mutation-tested: 3 tampering scenarios (SHA-swap on STALE, VERIFIED without
  artifact, VERIFIED with exit=1) all fail the gate (exit 1).

This commit is docs/tests-only: product tree untouched (validator enforces).
